course: dictionary
lesson: 6556
title: Ng: one sound, two letters
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A digraph is two letters that make one sound. The pair «ng» is one of them: it makes the sound you hear at the end of sing, ring and long. Say sing slowly. The n and the g do not give you two separate sounds; they blend into one.
explain: Look at «king», «song» and «thing». In each word, ng sits at the end and gives one sound. Try the sentence «The bell will ring.» Ring ends with the same sound as sing.
explain: On its own, «ng» is not a word. It is a letter pair, like sh, ch and th. A trigraph is three letters making one sound, such as igh in night.
explain: Context matters for «NG». In a text message, «That plan is NG» means «no good». In science, ng is short for nanogram, a billionth of a gram. The words around it tell you which meaning is right.
fact: A digraph is two letters making one sound.
fact: «ng» is a digraph heard in king, song, thing and sing.
fact: The letter pair «ng» is not a word on its own.
fact: «NG» in texts means «no good», as in «that plan is NG».
fact: In science, «ng» is short for nanogram, a billionth of a gram.
exercise: Which word ends with the same sound as «sing»? | rug | bell | *ring | rib
exercise: How many sounds do the letters «ng» make in «ring»? | No sound at all | Two sounds, n and g | *One sound | Three sounds
exercise: «That plan is NG» is written in a text message. What does NG mean? | National Guard | nanogram | Nigeria | *no good
test: Two letters that make one sound are called what? | abbreviation | trigraph | *digraph | nanogram
test: In science, what does «ng» usually mean? | *A nanogram, a billionth of a gram | No good | A member of the National Guard | A letter sound at the start of a word
exam: Which word has the «ng» sound at the end? | *sing | sun | sit | sap
